# ─── Supabase → Project Settings → API Keys ──────────────────────────────────
# "Publishable and secret API keys" tab.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co

# The Publishable key — starts with sb_publishable_. Safe in the browser.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# ─── Supabase → Connect → Transaction pooler ─────────────────────────────────
# Use the pooler (port 6543), not the direct connection on 5432: serverless
# functions open far too many connections for Postgres to handle directly.
# Replace [YOUR-PASSWORD] with the database password you set at project creation.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.YOUR-PROJECT-REF:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-1-REGION.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres

# ─── Optional ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Secret key — starts with sb_secret_. Only needed for `npm run demo`.
# It bypasses every access control in the project: never expose it to the
# browser, never set it in a deployed environment, never commit it.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...

# ─── Optional: log signups/logins to a Google Sheet (lib/logAuthEvent.ts) ────
# Appends [ISO timestamp, email, event] to a sheet you own. Passwords are never
# logged. Delivery is a POST to a Google Apps Script web app bound to the sheet
# — no service account. Setup steps are in lib/logAuthEvent.ts.
# SIGNUP_WEBHOOK_URL=https://script.google.com/macros/s/…/exec
# SIGNUP_WEBHOOK_SECRET=some-random-string   # optional; verify it in doPost

# ─── Optional: pin the origin OAuth comes back to (lib/siteUrl.ts) ───────────
# Google sends the reader back through Supabase to an absolute URL, which is
# normally worked out from the request's own Host — right on localhost and
# right on Vercel, with no configuration. Set this only if something in front
# of the app rewrites Host. No trailing slash.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://far-east-beta.vercel.app
